Subject: [PATCH] overlayfs: add xino-style identity for read-only LG unions

LG mounts /product as a read-only overlay whose lower layers live on
different filesystems.  This 4.9 overlayfs predates xino support, so its
getattr implementation returns the lower filesystem's st_dev for regular
files while directories return the overlay superblock's st_dev.  Besides
making a single tree appear to cross devices, that makes filesystem scanners
report every APK, ODEX and VDEX below /product as an inconsistent mount.

Use the overlay superblock device for objects on read-only overlay mounts,
but also encode the real device in the high 32 bits of st_ino.  The latter is
essential: changing st_dev alone can collapse distinct (st_dev, st_ino) pairs
from different lower filesystems into the same identity.  If the real inode
does not fit in 32 bits, retain the original identity, matching upstream
xino's safe overflow fallback.  Writable overlays retain the upstream 4.9
behavior, where preserving the real layer identity can matter during copy-up.

diff --git a/fs/overlayfs/inode.c b/fs/overlayfs/inode.c
--- a/fs/overlayfs/inode.c
+++ b/fs/overlayfs/inode.c
@@ -116,6 +116,19 @@ static int ovl_getattr(struct vfsmount *mnt, struct dentry *dentry,
 	old_cred = ovl_override_creds(dentry->d_sb);
 	err = vfs_getattr(&realpath, stat);
 	ovl_revert_creds(old_cred);
+
+	/*
+	 * Give small lower inode numbers a unified, collision-free identity like
+	 * upstream xino: preserve the real device in high inode bits, then expose
+	 * the overlay device.  Merely replacing st_dev is unsafe because two lower
+	 * filesystems can contain the same inode number.  Keep the real identity on
+	 * overflow and leave writable/copy-up overlays on the original 4.9 path.
+	 */
+	if (!err && (dentry->d_sb->s_flags & MS_RDONLY) &&
+	    stat->dev != dentry->d_sb->s_dev && !(stat->ino >> 32)) {
+		stat->ino |= (u64)stat->dev << 32;
+		stat->dev = dentry->d_sb->s_dev;
+	}
 	return err;
 }
 
